  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday night through Sunday)\nIssued at 313 AM EDT Mon Aug 10 2026\n\nOver the course of the long term period, ridging initially situated \natop the Desert Southwest will translate eastward, stagnating over \nthe Southeast for several days. In the absence of stronger \nkinematics, any disturbances traversing mid-upper flow may help to \nlocally bolster convective coverage (or perhaps intensity) but by \nand large, scattered to numerous garden variety summertime \nthunderstorms are expected each afternoon through the extended \nrange. Moisture streaming off of the Gulf will support dewpoints in \nthe mid-to-upper 70s, sufficient to support progressively more \noppressive heat from midweek on. Highs on Wednesday are progged to \nremain largely seasonable, in the upper 80s to mid 90s (within a \ncouple degrees of norms). However, air temperatures will return to \nthe 90s areawide by the weekend. As such, heat index values will \nsurge into the triple digits. Heat Advisory criteria is likely to be \nmet for at least subsets of the eastern portion of the area, and \nconditions will need to be monitored for potential Extreme Heat \nproducts assuming trends continue. Either way, make next weekend's \nplans with a high likelihood of impactful heat in mind.",
